% LL and superscript UL, and trailing subscript LR and superscript UR.
% Omitting an argument suppresses it. Safe in text, inline, and display mode.
%
% Every script is wrapped in the macro `zscript-wrapper` when it is stored. The
% option is mode-free and takes any macro accepting one argument, but three
% settings are recommended, each with its own caveats:
%   \symup  (default) math letters, Greek letters, digits and signs are typed
%           as they are and set upright; a variable needs \symit{...}, and a
%           label with spaces or hyphens needs \text{...}.
%   \text   labels are typed as they are; a variable, Greek letter or sign
%           needs $...$.
%   (empty) scripts are set in the ambient math alphabet, as plain TeX would;
%           a label needs \text{...}.
