% than `true` counts as false) selects how scripts are placed. True: from the
% edges of the nucleus, as described below. False: by TeX itself, as if typed
% {}_{LL}^{UL} {nucleus}_{LR}^{UR}, i.e. hanging from the baseline by font
% parameters (the traditional placement). A large operator then still takes
% its scripts at the sides in every style (like \nolimits), and no space is
% added between leading scripts and the nucleus. The position and frame
% options are ignored; the wrapper and the star scaling still apply.
%
