% `zscript-adaptative` true the call is placed by TeX, with it false the call
% is placed from the edges of the nucleus. The + must directly follow the
% command name; a nucleus that is a lone + must be braced, {+}.
%
% When adaptative, scripts are boxes placed explicitly, never by TeX's script
% machinery, so they are free to overlap the nucleus. An unstarred script is
% set one style smaller than the nucleus. A star before a script additionally
% scales it by `zscript-scale-<style>`, where <style> (display, text, script,
% scriptscript) is the style of the NUCLEUS; the same four factors apply to
